# github-projects (Cursor)

Works on any board. Wave is the only sequencing field. Full rules:
`references/model.md`.

## Board first

Ask for the board URL (`https://github.com/orgs/<org>/projects/<n>`) if not
given. Never default, never infer from the repo, never reuse another
session's board. Pass `--project <URL>` to every script.

- New board: `node scripts/new-board.mjs --org <org> --title "..." --applications "A,B"`
  (copies the org Wave template, views included).
- Board without a Wave field: ask, then `node scripts/init-board.mjs --project <URL>`
  (adds fields; views via web UI), or follow that board's own rules.
- Board/field/view changes need the user's explicit approval.

## Fields

Status (Backlog/Ready/In Progress/Done), Wave (Tracking, W0..Wn, mandatory),
Application (the board's own apps, distinct colors, mandatory), Assignees
(mandatory), Start Date / Target Date, Estimate (jam). Tracking = umbrella items.

## New work: subtask or new Wave

Never a loose item. Weigh with `references/subtask-vs-wave.md`:
subtask when same goal as an existing [Wn], <= 8h or <= 30% of that Wave,
one issue, no new app/major schema. Otherwise new Wave. Recommend one with
reasons, then let the user decide. No fitting parent: show candidates, ask.

## Issue

Title `[Wn] ...` or `[Wn-follow-up] ...`.
Header: `Wave: Wn | Parent: o/r#n | Repo: o/r | Branch: <branch> (from <base>) | Depends: ...`.
Sections: 1. Definition, 2. Changes, 3. Success Criteria (Functional, Test
mandatory, Regression checkboxes), optional 4. Keputusan terbuka.
Subtask = real GitHub sub-issue of its [Wn] parent. Done parent stays Done.
If Depends not Done, stay Backlog.

## Scripts (dry run unless --yes, all take --project <URL>)

`new-board.mjs`, `init-board.mjs`, `next-task.mjs`, `add-subtask.mjs --parent o/r#n --title ...`,
`set-fields.mjs o/r#n --wave W2 ...`, `set-status.mjs o/r#n "In Progress"`,
`mark-done.mjs o/r#n`, `lint-board.mjs`, `wave-report.mjs`, `setup-template.mjs`.
See `scripts/README.md`.

## Views

All grouped by Wave: All Work Items (table), Engineering Workflow (board by
Status, swimlanes Wave), Delivery Roadmap (Start Date → Target Date),
Development Wave (table, `-wave:Tracking`). Copied boards have them;
initialized boards need the web UI. See `references/views.md`.
